  "rationale": "With no defences, exfiltration is reachable: phish_workstation gives foothold_workstation and stolen_user; pivot_internal gives reach_internal; auth_appserver, then kerberoast_dc gives stolen_admin; auth_dc and escalate_dc give admin_dc; dump_dbadmin_dc gives stolen_dbadmin; then auth_db, escalate_db and exfiltrate_db. So 0 controls is not enough. Deploying mfa:admin alone is sufficient. stolen_dbadmin can only come from dump_dbadmin_dc or dump_dbadmin_adfs, which need admin_dc or admin_adfs. Those need foothold_dc or foothold_adfs, and the only ways to get them are auth_dc and auth_adfs, both of which require NOT mfa_admin. Without stolen_dbadmin, auth_db, auth_fileserver and auth_backup are all blocked. So admin_db, admin_fileserver and admin_backup are unreachable, and every exfiltrate technique is blocked. The minimum is therefore 1."
